  26:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     [..]
  29:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       The SPI HAL driver can be used as follows:
  30:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  31:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Declare a SPI_HandleTypeDef handle structure, for example:
  32:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           SPI_HandleTypeDef  hspi;
  33:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  34:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#)Initialize the SPI low level resources by implementing the HAL_SPI_MspInit() API:
  35:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) Enable the SPIx interface clock
  36:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) SPI pins configuration
  37:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Enable the clock for the SPI GPIOs
  38:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure these SPI pins as alternate function push-pull
  39:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process or DMA process
  40:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the SPIx interrupt priority
  41:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Enable the NVIC SPI IRQ handle
  42:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (##) DMA Configuration if you need to use DMA process
  43:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Declare a DMA_HandleTypeDef handle structure for the transmit or receive Stream
  44:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Enable the DMAx clock
  45:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the DMA handle parameters
  46:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the DMA Tx or Rx Stream/Channel
  47:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Associate the initialized hdma_tx handle to the hspi DMA Tx or Rx handle
  48:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               (+++) Configure the priority and enable the NVIC for the transfer complete interrupt 
  49:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****                     or Rx Stream/Channel
  50:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  51:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Program the Mode, BidirectionalMode , Data size, Baudrate Prescaler, NSS
  52:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           management, Clock polarity and phase, FirstBit and CRC configuration in the hspi Init str
  53:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  54:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Initialize the SPI registers by calling the HAL_SPI_Init() API:
  55:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (++) This API configures also the low level Hardware GPIO, CLOCK, CORTEX...etc)
  56:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****               by calling the customized HAL_SPI_MspInit() API.
  57:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****      [..]
  58:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        Callback registration:
  59:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  60:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) The compilation flag USE_HAL_SPI_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1UL
  61:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
  62:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           Use Functions HAL_SPI_RegisterCallback() to register an interrupt callback.
  63:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  64:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           Function HAL_SPI_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
  65:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxCpltCallback        : SPI Tx Completed callback
  66:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxCpltCallback        : SPI Rx Completed callback
  67:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxCpltCallback      : SPI TxRx Completed callback
  68:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Tx Half Completed callback
  69:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Rx Half Completed callback
  70:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxHalfCpltCallback  : SPI TxRx Half Completed callback
  71:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) ErrorCallback         : SPI Error callback
  72:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) AbortCpltCallback     : SPI Abort callback
  73:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) SuspendCallback       : SPI Suspend callback
  74:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspInitCallback       : SPI Msp Init callback
  75:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspDeInitCallback     : SPI Msp DeInit callback
  76:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
  77:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           and a pointer to the user callback function.
  78:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  79:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  80:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (#) Use function HAL_SPI_UnRegisterCallback to reset a callback to the default
  81:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           weak function.
  82:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           HAL_SPI_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
ARM GAS  /tmp/claude-1000/ccrjL7tu.s 			page 3


  83:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           and the Callback ID.
  84:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           This function allows to reset following callbacks:
  85:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxCpltCallback        : SPI Tx Completed callback
  86:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxCpltCallback        : SPI Rx Completed callback
  87:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxCpltCallback      : SPI TxRx Completed callback
  88:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Tx Half Completed callback
  89:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) RxHalfCpltCallback    : SPI Rx Half Completed callback
  90:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) TxRxHalfCpltCallback  : SPI TxRx Half Completed callback
  91:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) ErrorCallback         : SPI Error callback
  92:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) AbortCpltCallback     : SPI Abort callback
  93:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) SuspendCallback       : SPI Suspend callback
  94:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspInitCallback       : SPI Msp Init callback
  95:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             (++) MspDeInitCallback     : SPI Msp DeInit callback
  96:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
  97:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        By default, after the HAL_SPI_Init() and when the state is HAL_SPI_STATE_RESET
  98:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
  99:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        examples HAL_SPI_MasterTxCpltCallback(), HAL_SPI_MasterRxCpltCallback().
 100:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 101:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_SPI_Init()/ HAL_SPI_DeInit() only when
 102:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 103:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        If MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SPI_Init()/ HAL_SPI_DeInit()
 104:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand) whatever the state
 105:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 106:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_SPI_STATE_READY state only.
 107:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit functions that can be registered/unregistered
 108:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        in HAL_SPI_STATE_READY or HAL_SPI_STATE_RESET state,
 109:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 110:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        Then, the user first registers the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 111:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        using HAL_SPI_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_SPI_DeInit()
 112:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        or HAL_SPI_Init() function.
 113:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 114:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        When The compilation define USE_HAL_PPP_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or not defined,
 115:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        the callback registering feature is not available and weak callbacks are used.
 116:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 117:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        SuspendCallback restriction:
 118:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****            SuspendCallback is called only when MasterReceiverAutoSusp is enabled and
 119:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        EOT interrupt is activated. SuspendCallback is used in relation with functions
 120:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        HAL_SPI_Transmit_IT, HAL_SPI_Receive_IT and HAL_SPI_TransmitReceive_IT.
 121:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 122:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     [..]
 123:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       Circular mode restriction:
 124:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (+) The DMA circular mode cannot be used when the SPI is configured in these modes:
 125:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (++) Master 2Lines RxOnly
 126:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           (++) Master 1Line Rx
 127:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (+) The CRC feature is not managed when the DMA circular mode is enabled
 128:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****       (+) The functions HAL_SPI_DMAPause()/ HAL_SPI_DMAResume() are not supported. Return always
 129:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           HAL_ERROR with ErrorCode set to HAL_SPI_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED.
 130:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****           Those functions are maintained for backward compatibility reasons.
 131:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 132:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****   @endverbatim
 133:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****   */
 134:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 135:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** /* Includes ------------------------------------------------------------------*/
