 796:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** /** @defgroup SPI_Exported_Functions_Group2 IO operation functions
 797:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****   *  @brief   Data transfers functions
 798:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****   *
 799:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** @verbatim
 800:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****   ==============================================================================
 801:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****                       ##### IO operation functions #####
 802:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****  ===============================================================================
 803:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****  [..]
 804:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the SPI
 805:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     data transfers.
 806:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 807:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     [..] The SPI supports master and slave mode :
 808:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 809:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
 810:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        (##) Blocking mode: The communication is performed in polling mode.
 811:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             The HAL status of all data processing is returned by the same function
 812:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             after finishing transfer.
 813:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****        (##) No-Blocking mode: The communication is performed using Interrupts
 814:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             or DMA, These APIs return the HAL status.
 815:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 816:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             dedicated SPI IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
 817:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             using DMA mode.
 818:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             The HAL_SPI_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_SPI_RxCpltCallback() and HAL_SPI_TxRxCpltCallback() u
 819:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             will be executed respectively at the end of the transmit or Receive process
 820:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****             The HAL_SPI_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a communication error is
 821:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 822:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****     (#) APIs provided for these 2 transfer modes (Blocking mode or Non blocking mode using either I
 823:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_spi.c ****         exist for 1Line (simplex) and 2Lines (full duplex) modes.
ARM GAS  /tmp/claude-1000/ccrjL7tu.s 			page 16


